ζηλωτής, -οῦ, ὁ
(ζηλόω), [in LXX for קַנָּא (θεὸς ζ.), Exo.20.5; 34.14, Deu.4.24; 5.9; 6.15; קַנּוֹא, Nam.1.2 (θεός); pl., I Est.8.72 ζ. τῶν νόμων, 2Ma.4.2τὸν ζ. Φινεές, 4Ma.18.12 (cf. Num.25.11)* ;] 
__1. in cl. an emulator, zealous admirer (Plat., al.). 
__2. eagerly desirous, zealous; 
__(a) absol., as in OT, ll. with; 
__(b) with genitive obj.: (zealous to acquire or to defend), 1Co.14.12, Tit.2.14, 1Pe.3.13; τ.…
